WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.133
[The Science and Art of Obstetrics]

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:17.799
[Laparotrachelotomy: Low, cervical cesarean section, by Joseph B. DeLee, M.D. and M. Edward Davis, M.D.]

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:25.200
[Taken at the Chicago Lying-In Hospital, Fox Movietone Scientific]

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:38.000
[...]

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:57.000
[Dr. DeLee appears, no audio present]

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.133
[Dr. DeLee:] ...in eighteen hundred and five.

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:02.099
And he did the operation,

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.433
he did the operation twice.

00:01:04.433 --> 00:01:06.899
Both of the patients died,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.333
but he realized that it was a step in advance,

00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:14.699
and recommended it for all cases
requiring abdominal delivery.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.666
The mortality of the
classic cesarean section

00:01:17.666 --> 00:01:21.432
has improved as
time has gone on,

00:01:21.433 --> 00:01:24.333
and it did not seem that we needed

00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:27.166
a better method of abdominal delivery.

00:01:27.166 --> 00:01:31.366
But, our ideas of what was good also improved.

00:01:31.366 --> 00:01:38.166
In 1870, the mortality of 15 percent in Cesarean section was not bad.

00:01:38.166 --> 00:01:42.799
In 1900, the mortality of four percent was considered excellent.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:48.400
In 1930, a mortality of one percent is too much.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:53.300
Therefore, when in 1906 Fritz Frank of Bonn

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:58.266
introduced the operation of Osiander,

00:01:58.266 --> 00:02:02.166
the low cervical incision, it was eagerly seized

00:02:02.166 --> 00:02:07.766
by the German operator, and its use has been spread over Europe

00:02:07.766 --> 00:02:11.232
and now in the United States, it likewise

00:02:11.233 --> 00:02:15.366
is receiving recognition.

00:02:15.366 --> 00:02:17.599
The principle of
the new operation

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.300
is that the incision is made in the lower uterine segment,

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.966
the neck of the uterus,

00:02:23.966 --> 00:02:26.066
and not in the fundus.

00:02:26.066 --> 00:02:29.266
And all the superiority
of the new operation

00:02:29.266 --> 00:02:38.466
grows out of this fact.

00:02:38.466 --> 00:02:42.899
There are two kinds of low cervical Cesarean:

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.866
one where the incision being made just above the pubis,

00:02:47.866 --> 00:02:49.832
approach to the
lower uterine segment

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:54.300
is gained by cutting through
the peritoneal cavity.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:03:00.333
This is called the
intraperitoneal method.

00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:03.533
The other kind is where the incision is made

00:03:03.533 --> 00:03:06.766
just above the pubis, and the peritoneum

00:03:06.766 --> 00:03:10.766
is pushed upward towards the navel...also the bladder.

00:03:10.766 --> 00:03:13.232
And the bladder is pushed to the side,

00:03:13.233 --> 00:03:16.766
and an area of lower uterine segment exposed,

00:03:16.766 --> 00:03:19.199
sufficiently large for
the delivery of the baby.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.066
This is called
extraperitoneal method,

00:03:22.066 --> 00:03:25.899
the general peritoneal
cavity not being opened.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:29.733
The majority of men prefer the direct route,

00:03:29.733 --> 00:03:32.933
the intraperitoneal method.

00:03:32.933 --> 00:03:37.433
The indications for the low
cervical Cesarean section

00:03:37.433 --> 00:03:41.633
are exactly the same as for
the classic Cesarean section.

00:03:41.633 --> 00:03:44.966
But owing to the safety
of the low operation,

00:03:44.966 --> 00:03:49.166
we can extend the field
in which it may be done.

00:03:49.166 --> 00:03:51.899
Now it is a fact that
in the United States,

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.633
too many Cesarean
sections are being done.

00:03:55.633 --> 00:03:59.899
And it is also a fact that if the new operation

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.200
were generally practiced, the total number

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.333
of Cesareans done in the
United States would be reduced.

00:04:05.333 --> 00:04:10.299
I shall have occasion to
refer to this point later on.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:15.200
The contraindications to
the operation are very few.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.633
In a woman with a
pendulous belly,

00:04:17.633 --> 00:04:22.199
it may be hard to get access to
the lower part of the abdomen

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.166
to make the incision.

00:04:24.166 --> 00:04:26.732
And if you are going
to do a Porro,

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:29.833
it is hardly worthwhile
to do the low operation.

00:04:29.833 --> 00:04:33.033
But if at any time you
have to do the old classic,

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:37.533
make it as low in the uterus as
possible so as to get as many

00:04:37.533 --> 00:04:43.433
of the advantages of the low
operation as are to be had.

00:04:43.433 --> 00:04:58.733
Now a few words about the surgical anatomy.

00:04:58.733 --> 00:05:04.433
Here is a model of a woman
at term, but not in labor.

00:05:04.433 --> 00:05:07.466
Here is the cervix, and here the lower uterine segment,

00:05:07.466 --> 00:05:11.799
which is about nine centimeters long.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:16.600
This is variable, but it nearly
always is long enough for you

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:19.200
to extract the baby through it.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:23.800
Here is the loop peritoneum over the lower uterine segment,

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.833
and here is the fascia, this white line,

00:05:26.833 --> 00:05:29.499
the fascia that
extended from the vagina

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:35.500
upward, and loses itself towards
the fundus of the uterus.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:39.866
It is about this point that
the grey seam is located.

00:05:39.866 --> 00:05:42.132
You will hear a great deal about the grey seam

00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:50.933
during the operation.

00:05:50.933 --> 00:05:55.333
Here is a model of a woman who
has been in the second stage

00:05:55.333 --> 00:05:57.333
for a long time.

00:05:57.333 --> 00:06:00.699
And you can see how long
and thin the lower uterine

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:03.000
segment and cervix are.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.900
They are fully 15 centimeters long,

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:10.900
and the lower uterine segment almost invites you to cut into it.

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.900
When you do your
first low cervical,

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.966
select the place
where the labor has

00:06:15.966 --> 00:06:18.466
been on for a considerable
length of time.

00:06:18.466 --> 00:06:21.166
And that makes it much easier.

00:06:21.166 --> 00:06:23.099
You see how thin it is.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.233
Here is the peritoneum again,

00:06:25.233 --> 00:06:29.833
and here is the contraction rate.

00:06:29.833 --> 00:06:36.733
Now gentlemen, a few words about local anesthesia.

00:06:36.733 --> 00:06:41.233
It is particularly well-adapted to the low cervical cesarean section

00:06:41.233 --> 00:06:44.333
And I prefer it to
the spinal anesthesia,

00:06:44.333 --> 00:06:47.666
indeed to general
anesthetics, too.

00:06:47.666 --> 00:06:50.532
No one can deny that
spinal anesthesia

00:06:50.533 --> 00:06:54.099
is more dangerous than
a local infiltration.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:57.566
And since we can, in 90 percent of the cases,

00:06:57.566 --> 00:07:00.632
succeed with local
infiltration anesthesia,

00:07:00.633 --> 00:07:02.433
this should be the
method of choice.

00:07:02.433 --> 00:07:04.733
And I have here in my
hand the instruments

00:07:04.733 --> 00:07:07.899
that we use at the
Chicago Lying-In Hospital.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:11.233
They facilitate the operation,
but ordinary syringes

00:07:11.233 --> 00:07:14.199
will do the work just as well.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:19.966
We use a novacaine-cocaine solution, one half of one percent,

00:07:19.966 --> 00:07:22.699
And we add two minims of adrenaline

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:25.066
to every ounce of the solution.

00:07:25.066 --> 00:07:29.399
We use seven or eight ounces, sometimes nine or ten,

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:31.733
and we have never had any cases of poisoning,

00:07:31.733 --> 00:07:33.966
or any trouble whatever.

00:07:33.966 --> 00:07:37.232
After the baby is born, a
quarter of a grain of morphine

00:07:37.233 --> 00:07:41.133
and 1/150th of scopolamine are given.

00:07:41.133 --> 00:07:45.966
Solomon said that you should
have an understanding heart.

00:07:45.966 --> 00:07:48.466
And this will help you a great deal in your

00:07:48.466 --> 00:07:50.332
operating under local anesthesia.

00:07:50.333 --> 00:07:54.033
No tugging, no pulling,
no jarring of the patient.

00:07:54.033 --> 00:07:57.166
Gentleness all the time,
and you will succeed.

00:07:57.166 --> 00:07:59.332
Now gentlemen, let us
proceed to the amphitheater

00:07:59.333 --> 00:08:02.233
where we will do the operation.

00:08:02.233 --> 00:08:05.266
Now Mrs. Herman, we
are ready to start.

00:08:05.266 --> 00:08:06.632
Don't be afraid.

00:08:06.633 --> 00:08:09.599
It will hurt just a little
when the baby comes.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:11.200
I'll prepare you.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:14.800
If any of my work should
give you pain, say ouch.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:20.500
But don't move.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:29.366
Pubis.

00:08:29.366 --> 00:08:37.699
Navel.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:42.600
We use a very fine needle to make a wheel in the skin.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:57.066
Then the big needle doesn't
hurt when it goes in.

00:08:57.066 --> 00:09:05.666
Inject the novocaine into the skin itself, and, of course,

00:09:05.666 --> 00:09:24.499
into the fascia
right under the skin.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:29.100
Inject as you move
the needle in and out.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:30.500
Do you feel that?

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.366
[Patient:] No.

00:09:32.366 --> 00:09:33.832
[Dr. DeLee:] Do you feel that?

00:09:33.833 --> 00:09:35.766
[Patient:] No, Doctor.

00:09:35.766 --> 00:09:36.699
[Dr. DeLee:] That's good.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:39.400
You're going to see the grey seam,

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:45.400
where the loose peritoneum
of the uterus becomes firmly
adherent.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:48.266
See how loose it is here?

00:09:48.266 --> 00:09:55.060
...but I prefer the scissors.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:10:06.080
[...]

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:10.560
On this drawing, you see where the clamps go,

00:10:10.566 --> 00:10:14.266
and how the scissors cut the lower uterus in the front.

00:10:14.266 --> 00:10:20.832
On this pelvis, you see how
the forceps are to be applied,

00:10:20.833 --> 00:10:22.166
and the head delivered.

00:10:22.166 --> 00:10:26.132
See the hammer
effect of the forceps.

00:10:26.133 --> 00:10:36.166
Slowly, no hurry.

00:10:36.166 --> 00:10:39.699
Now Mrs. Herman, the
baby is about to come.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.266
Be brave.

00:10:41.266 --> 00:10:42.899
Don't squirm.

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:44.700
Breathe quietly.

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:49.720
And in a very few moments, you will hear the baby cry.

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:55.400
[...]

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:58.433
I am putting my finger
in the baby's mouth

00:10:58.433 --> 00:10:59.933
to bring it to the front.

00:10:59.933 --> 00:11:00.833
Be careful,

00:11:00.833 --> 00:11:10.233
you can injure the little mouth.

00:11:10.233 --> 00:11:13.399
Wipe out the baby's mouth because if it gasps,

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:20.000
it might suck in the liquor amnii.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:28.500
[Baby crying]

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:32.433
Lift the forceps blade
under the lip of the womb.

00:11:32.433 --> 00:11:42.133
Be very careful of that.

00:11:42.133 --> 00:11:47.033
Take lots of time,
very slowly and gently.

00:11:47.033 --> 00:11:52.933
All the instruments have
been removed from the womb.

00:11:52.933 --> 00:11:53.866
Slow...

00:11:53.866 --> 00:11:56.299
Take lots of time.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:57.433
No hurry.

00:11:57.433 --> 00:12:39.933
[Baby crying]

00:12:39.933 --> 00:12:41.966
Be ready to [INAUDIBLE].

00:12:41.966 --> 00:12:49.666
Carmen, will you have a lap sponge [INAUDIBLE]

00:12:49.666 --> 00:12:54.599
[Baby crying]

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:57.866
Now Mrs. Herman,
you go to sleep.

00:12:57.866 --> 00:13:00.866
You have a fine, healthy baby.

00:13:00.866 --> 00:13:04.699
And also, you had a hypodermic.

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:09.833
Gentlemen, we will now proceed to the repair of the womb.

00:13:09.833 --> 00:13:13.966
In this animated drawing,
which Mr. Carlson made,

00:13:13.966 --> 00:13:22.566
you will see the
course of the suture.

00:13:22.566 --> 00:13:38.899
Avoid the mucosa.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:43.733
Swing the needle around.

00:13:43.733 --> 00:13:46.866
Now in the upper
part of the uterus,

00:13:46.866 --> 00:13:50.432
the muscle is much thicker
and is likely to retract up

00:13:50.433 --> 00:13:55.199
into the body of the uterus.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:58.900
[Observer;} What kind of suture material
do you use, Dr. DeLee?

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:02.600
[Dr. DeLee:] We use number two catgut for the first row.

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:05.500
The second row,
we use number one.

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:17.566
And for the peritoneum, number one.

00:14:17.566 --> 00:14:20.932
Very important to get a good apposition here,

00:14:20.933 --> 00:14:24.599
in order to have a firm
scar in the lower portion

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:36.933
of the fundus and the cervix.

00:14:36.933 --> 00:14:45.566
Don't catch the gauze in the needle.

00:14:45.566 --> 00:14:48.499
Pull it out a little there.

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:51.400
The complications of the third stage...

00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:54.133
very seldom is there
post-partum hemorrhage

00:14:54.133 --> 00:14:56.666
in laparotrachelotomy,

00:14:56.666 --> 00:14:59.232
especially if you use local anesthesia.

00:14:59.233 --> 00:15:01.599
And we give ergot 15 minutes

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:04.766
before the baby is
born, and a [INAUDIBLE]

00:15:04.766 --> 00:15:06.832
pituitary right afterwards.

00:15:06.833 --> 00:15:09.466
If there should be hemorrhage,
we pack the uterus.

00:15:09.466 --> 00:15:11.566
But I do that as a routine.

00:15:11.566 --> 00:15:13.832
And if you wanted
to give pituitary

00:15:13.833 --> 00:15:20.399
as it's been necessary, inject it under the peritoneum as...

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:22.500
I put it under the peritoneum.

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:25.466
because if the solution is infected and makes an abscess,

00:15:25.466 --> 00:15:32.199
the abscess is not open
into the peritoneal cavity.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:36.933
Some accoucheurs believe
that placenta previa is not

00:15:36.933 --> 00:15:40.866
a good indication for
laparotrachelotomy.

00:15:40.866 --> 00:15:45.499
But our experience in 40
cases without mortality

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.566
proves the contrary.

00:15:47.566 --> 00:15:52.632
There are three or possibly four things that must be remembered.

00:15:52.633 --> 00:15:56.433
In the first place,
in anemic cases

00:15:56.433 --> 00:16:00.399
precede the operation by
a transfusion of blood.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:04.466
And second, save blood
throughout the whole course

00:16:04.466 --> 00:16:05.766
of the operation.

00:16:05.766 --> 00:16:07.532
Don't waste any.

00:16:07.533 --> 00:16:11.133
Third, deliver the baby
by version and extraction,

00:16:11.133 --> 00:16:16.399
and proceed slowly so as
not to do any tearing.

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:19.600
Fourth, clamp all
the bleeding vessels,

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:23.533
and hold them securely clamped
until they are sutured.

00:16:23.533 --> 00:16:28.066
Now gentlemen, do not
fear the difficulties

00:16:28.066 --> 00:16:29.832
that you might encounter.

00:16:29.833 --> 00:16:32.299
The field is open before you,

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:35.800
and you can meet the emergencies as they arise.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:40.933
The hemorrhage, you can control by the ordinary tools and surgical method.

00:16:40.933 --> 00:16:45.533
And mechanical difficulties
are overcome by taking time,

00:16:45.533 --> 00:16:49.733
and by art instead of strength.

00:16:49.733 --> 00:16:53.333
Let me again recommend
the low cervical cesarean

00:16:53.333 --> 00:16:59.833
or laparotrachelotomy, as
well as the local anesthesia.

00:16:59.833 --> 00:17:03.166
Any of the difficulties, an
ordinarily skilled surgeon

00:17:03.166 --> 00:17:04.766
can overcome.

00:17:04.766 --> 00:17:07.732
And if you will perform
this operation as a routine,

00:17:07.733 --> 00:17:11.966
I am sure that you will
cut your mortality in half.

00:17:11.966 --> 00:17:16.299
What are the particular
features of the low cesarean

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:18.566
that make it so superior?

00:17:18.566 --> 00:17:24.332
As I said before the operation,
these points of superiority

00:17:24.333 --> 00:17:27.099
grow out of the fact
that the incision is

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.666
in the lower uterine segment.

00:17:29.666 --> 00:17:40.266
And I will now give you 10 of
these points of superiority.

00:17:40.266 --> 00:17:45.399
The first point is that the
incision is in the lower

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:47.433
part of the abdomen.

00:17:47.433 --> 00:17:50.366
All the surgeons know
that the lower abdomen

00:17:50.366 --> 00:17:55.366
is more resistant to infection than the upper abdomen.

00:17:55.366 --> 00:18:01.132
The intestines and the omentum will rarely come into view,

00:18:01.133 --> 00:18:02.999
and are not touched.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:07.533
Therefore, shock is small,

00:18:07.533 --> 00:18:12.866
and there is less tendency to vomiting after the delivery,

00:18:12.866 --> 00:18:15.032
and to ileus.

00:18:15.033 --> 00:18:20.999
The spill is located
right around the womb

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.700
and has very little
distribution,

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:29.500
which also helps prevent shock, ileus, and nausea

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.300
and vomiting.

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:33.900
The cervix, in which the incision is made,

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:39.933
is more resistant to infection, being used to it.

00:18:39.933 --> 00:18:44.933
Every gynecologist knows how
much the cervix can stand.

00:18:44.933 --> 00:18:54.966
I will now show you
this on another chart.

00:18:54.966 --> 00:18:57.632
This chart shows the delivery...

00:18:57.633 --> 00:19:00.766
shows the uterus a few
hours after delivery.

00:19:00.766 --> 00:19:05.866
As you see, the cervix shrinks
and drops into the pelvis,

00:19:05.866 --> 00:19:08.566
out of the general
peritoneal cavity.

00:19:08.566 --> 00:19:10.099
This was point five.

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:19.533
Point six. In this chart you see the uterus a few hours after delivery.

00:19:19.533 --> 00:19:23.066
And as you will notice,
the wound in the cervix

00:19:23.066 --> 00:19:27.466
has dropped down into the
cavity of the pelvis, far away

00:19:27.466 --> 00:19:32.266
from the general peritoneal cavity.

00:19:32.266 --> 00:19:36.699
That was point five in
the list of superiority.

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:41.433
One of the greatest
advantages of the low incision

00:19:41.433 --> 00:19:46.033
lies in the security of the
scar in subsequent pregnancies

00:19:46.033 --> 00:19:47.533
and labors.

00:19:47.533 --> 00:19:52.766
Only a few cases of rupture
of the scar during pregnancy

00:19:52.766 --> 00:19:54.999
have been put on record.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:59.733
And the number of ruptures of
this scar during actual labor

00:19:59.733 --> 00:20:02.466
is only a small
fraction of those

00:20:02.466 --> 00:20:07.832
that occur after the
classic cesarean section.

00:20:07.833 --> 00:20:11.099
The reason for this
security from rupture

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:15.400
is easily seen by a
reference to these charts.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:21.333
In this operation, the wound is in the lower uterine segment,

00:20:21.333 --> 00:20:24.833
which is at rest and
can heal in peace.

00:20:24.833 --> 00:20:30.699
It is not disturbed by the turmoil going on in the fundus above.

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:36.866
Compare that wound with this, after the classic cesarean section.

00:20:36.866 --> 00:20:40.132
Here, the wound
is in the fundus,

00:20:40.133 --> 00:20:43.733
which is in a constant
state of unrest.

00:20:43.733 --> 00:20:47.066
The uterine contractions,
the afterpain,

00:20:47.066 --> 00:20:49.599
keep up a constant motion,

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:53.933
and sooner or later, one of these stitches or more

00:20:53.933 --> 00:20:59.833
[INAUDIBLE] will tear, and
let the cut, the lochia

00:20:59.833 --> 00:21:05.099
and bacteria into the wound
and into the peritoneal cavity.

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:08.100
Point of superiority,
number seven.

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:10.800
In the old classic cesarean,

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:14.333
the lochia has a chance to seep through the uterus

00:21:14.333 --> 00:21:20.533
into the general peritoneal
cavity, causing peritonitis.

00:21:20.533 --> 00:21:23.733
In the new operation,
the low cervical,

00:21:23.733 --> 00:21:27.866
the lochia is prevented
from seeping through,

00:21:27.866 --> 00:21:31.666
and is confined to the
neighborhood of the cervix

00:21:31.666 --> 00:21:35.732
and under the bladder.

00:21:35.733 --> 00:21:39.599
Should infection occur,
which is not common,

00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:44.633
see how easy it is to drain
the area that is infected.

00:21:44.633 --> 00:21:48.233
Either you can pull the
cervix down with a vulsellum

00:21:48.233 --> 00:21:50.799
and make an anterior colpotomy,

00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:54.033
thus reaching the abscess under the bladder,

00:21:54.033 --> 00:21:58.433
or you can burrow a finger through the stitches,

00:21:58.433 --> 00:22:00.333
into the abscess.

00:22:00.333 --> 00:22:05.033
Or, what is most common, nature helps you

00:22:05.033 --> 00:22:12.633
in that the pus burrows under the bladder, around the bladder,

00:22:12.633 --> 00:22:15.266
through the cavity urethras.

00:22:15.266 --> 00:22:18.699
And by taking out one, two
or three of these stitches,

00:22:18.700 --> 00:22:20.466
you can let the pus out,

00:22:20.466 --> 00:22:28.032
and usually, healing is very rapid and complete.

00:22:28.033 --> 00:22:30.799
For comparison, see
where the infection

00:22:30.800 --> 00:22:36.266
would travel after a
classic cesarean section,

00:22:36.266 --> 00:22:44.599
beginning here in the endometrium,

00:22:44.600 --> 00:22:53.000
all through the peritoneal cavity.

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:58.066
Adhesions are common after the classic cesarean section,

00:22:58.066 --> 00:23:02.232
and the reason is very plain.

00:23:02.233 --> 00:23:06.433
Then the infection and pus is in
the intestines and the omentum.

00:23:06.433 --> 00:23:11.233
On the other hand, after the low operation,

00:23:11.233 --> 00:23:13.799
adhesions are very rare,

00:23:13.800 --> 00:23:15.800
and you can see why.

00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:19.000
The wound is dropped down into the pelvis, far away

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:21.366
from the general peritoneal cavity,

00:23:21.366 --> 00:23:25.166
and the omentum almost never comes down so low,

00:23:25.166 --> 00:23:27.832
the intestines hardly ever.

00:23:27.833 --> 00:23:33.366
And when the bladder fills, the peritoneal line of suture,

00:23:33.366 --> 00:23:36.466
that little line of suture I showed you at the operation,

00:23:36.466 --> 00:23:39.466
drops down into
a deep cul-de-sac

00:23:39.466 --> 00:23:42.499
and is further protected.

00:23:42.500 --> 00:23:45.500
Finally here, but there are many other reasons.

00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:49.200
The classical cesarean section is only safe

00:23:49.200 --> 00:23:51.633
when it is an operation of election.

00:23:51.633 --> 00:23:53.866
We can give a woman
a good test of labor,

00:23:53.866 --> 00:23:57.632
and then perform a low
cervical cesarean section.

00:23:57.633 --> 00:24:00.299
And therefore, by giving
a woman a test of labor,

00:24:00.300 --> 00:24:03.466
a great many cesareans will be unnecessary,

00:24:03.466 --> 00:24:06.299
and thus, the total percentage in the United States

00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:07.366
will be reduced.

00:24:07.366 --> 00:24:12.699
Now gentlemen, in conclusion, I have here the mortality statistics

00:24:12.700 --> 00:24:16.933
of the United States Census Bureau in Washington.

00:24:16.933 --> 00:24:19.833
And from these
tables we can learn

00:24:19.833 --> 00:24:25.533
that over 500 women die from
cesarean section every year.

00:24:25.533 --> 00:24:28.666
This is an enormous
number, and brings upon us

00:24:28.666 --> 00:24:31.299
the opprobrium of the community,

00:24:31.300 --> 00:24:34.466
when our statistics of maternal mortality

00:24:34.466 --> 00:24:37.699
are compared with those of other nations.

00:24:37.700 --> 00:24:42.733
If laparotrachelotomy was generally practiced in the United States,

00:24:42.733 --> 00:24:47.866
I am sure that most of this mortality would be reduced.

00:24:47.866 --> 00:24:49.832
And this is the reason that I have spent

00:24:49.833 --> 00:24:53.499
a great deal of time, a great deal of effort,

00:24:53.500 --> 00:24:55.600
and not a little
money in spreading

00:24:55.600 --> 00:24:58.866
the gospel of the low
cervical cesarean section,

00:24:58.866 --> 00:25:02.366
or laparotrachelotomy.

00:25:02.366 --> 00:25:23.266
[bells ringing]

00:25:23.266 --> 00:25:27.066
Ladies and gentlemen,
it is now six years

00:25:27.066 --> 00:25:30.399
since the picture which
you just saw was published.

00:25:30.400 --> 00:25:34.233
And I am going to tell you what has happened to the operation,

00:25:34.233 --> 00:25:37.499
laparotrachelotomy, during this time.

00:25:37.500 --> 00:25:41.566
But first, I want to
show you those babies.

00:25:41.566 --> 00:25:49.466
Boys, will you come in?

00:25:49.466 --> 00:25:52.366
I believe that Cesones do better

00:25:52.366 --> 00:25:57.399
mentally and physically than children delivered from below.

00:25:57.400 --> 00:26:07.866
Attention, salute,
left face, march.

00:26:07.866 --> 00:26:09.532
What has happened
to the operation

00:26:09.533 --> 00:26:11.966
during these six years?

00:26:11.966 --> 00:26:14.732
Several modifications
have been suggested,

00:26:14.733 --> 00:26:16.233
and we have tried them.

00:26:16.233 --> 00:26:18.099
But we have found
that the method

00:26:18.100 --> 00:26:20.200
which you saw on the screen,

00:26:20.200 --> 00:26:25.566
and which was perfected after 14 years of trial, is still the best.

00:26:25.566 --> 00:26:39.132
For example, the transverse surgical incision, like this.

00:26:39.133 --> 00:26:41.999
A transverse, curvilinear incision

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:48.466
is made above the bladder.

00:26:48.466 --> 00:26:52.699
We tried the operation
10 times, and gave it up.

00:26:52.700 --> 00:26:57.133
One severe hemorrhage from the
base of the broad ligament,

00:26:57.133 --> 00:27:00.199
one dangerous
extension of the womb,

00:27:00.200 --> 00:27:03.900
a big baby, twice difficulty

00:27:03.900 --> 00:27:06.900
in suturing the upper
to the lower flap.

00:27:06.900 --> 00:27:09.600
The upper muscular lamellae

00:27:09.600 --> 00:27:12.700
had retracted into the funds of the uterus,

00:27:12.700 --> 00:27:19.466
and one almost fatal pulmonary embolism.

00:27:19.466 --> 00:27:23.232
The literature records the fact that there are

00:27:23.233 --> 00:27:27.633
more pulmonary embolisms after the transverse incision

00:27:27.633 --> 00:27:29.866
than after the longitudinal.

00:27:29.866 --> 00:27:34.066
We had one embolism in
10 transverse incisions,

00:27:34.066 --> 00:27:40.166
and we had only one
embolism in the 1,800

00:27:40.166 --> 00:27:42.799
other laprotrachelotomies.

00:27:42.800 --> 00:27:46.466
The surgeons or gynecologists
would be very happy

00:27:46.466 --> 00:27:51.766
if they could record 1,800 consecutive laparotomies

00:27:51.766 --> 00:27:54.966
with only one
pulmonary embolism.

00:27:54.966 --> 00:28:03.632
This is the median incision.

00:28:03.633 --> 00:28:08.099
If the baby is large, you
can extend it up or down

00:28:08.100 --> 00:28:09.666
towards the cervix.

00:28:09.666 --> 00:28:13.432
If a tear occurs, it does
not go into the basis

00:28:13.433 --> 00:28:18.499
of the broad ligament where the big vessels and the urethra are.

00:28:18.500 --> 00:28:20.866
If the wound should
get infected,

00:28:20.866 --> 00:28:27.399
the dangerous areas, the big veins, are far away.

00:28:27.400 --> 00:28:30.600
[Observer:] Doctor, do you still use packing?

00:28:30.600 --> 00:28:31.733
[Dr. DeLee:] Oh, yes.

00:28:31.733 --> 00:28:34.299
We pack the uterus routinely.

00:28:34.300 --> 00:28:39.266
But we are now using
acriflavine, iodine,

00:28:39.266 --> 00:28:41.599
and glycerine on the gauze.

00:28:41.600 --> 00:28:46.400
I wonder if there really is
an antiseptic that does good.

00:28:46.400 --> 00:28:49.500
But we have a better ergot preparation.

00:28:49.500 --> 00:28:54.666
It is called ergonovine.

00:28:54.666 --> 00:28:57.832
Regarding post-operative
adhesions,

00:28:57.833 --> 00:29:01.466
we have done second and
third laprotrachelotomies

00:29:01.466 --> 00:29:04.399
on 345 patients.

00:29:04.400 --> 00:29:08.400
And we found adhesions
to be the exception.

00:29:08.400 --> 00:29:11.700
Whereas, after the classic cesarean section,

00:29:11.700 --> 00:29:13.500
adhesions are the rule.

00:29:13.500 --> 00:29:19.200
And they not seldom cause
serious late complications.

00:29:19.200 --> 00:29:22.000
Fertility, likewise,
is not compromised

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:27.733
by the low operation as
it is by the classic.

00:29:27.733 --> 00:29:31.499
Rupture of the uterus in subsequent pregnancy and labor...

00:29:31.500 --> 00:29:35.600
the cervical scar has
proven its superiority.

00:29:35.600 --> 00:29:39.333
There are only three cases on
record of rupture of the scar

00:29:39.333 --> 00:29:40.833
during pregnancy.

00:29:40.833 --> 00:29:44.933
And during labor, there are
less than 50 cases on record.

00:29:44.933 --> 00:29:48.066
Whereas the classic
cesarean is notoriously

00:29:48.066 --> 00:29:50.166
dangerous in this respect.

00:29:50.166 --> 00:29:54.366
There are thousands of
ruptures to its discredit.

00:29:54.366 --> 00:29:58.099
[Observer:] Doctor, how about placenta previa?

00:29:58.100 --> 00:30:02.700
[Dr. DeLee:] We have done 120 laprotrachelotomies

00:30:02.700 --> 00:30:05.966
in placenta previa without a single death.

00:30:05.966 --> 00:30:10.632
Some doctors claim that the
classic cesarean section

00:30:10.633 --> 00:30:14.166
is better in this complication.

00:30:14.166 --> 00:30:17.699
But we believe
just the opposite.

00:30:17.700 --> 00:30:20.233
We want to make the
opening in the uterus

00:30:20.233 --> 00:30:23.933
over the bed of the placenta, where we can attack

00:30:23.933 --> 00:30:26.966
a hemorrhage should one occur.

00:30:26.966 --> 00:30:32.699
You make the incision a little bit higher on the uterus than usual.

00:30:32.700 --> 00:30:35.733
The bleeding is only marked
if the placenta happens

00:30:35.733 --> 00:30:38.266
to be on the anterior wall.

00:30:38.266 --> 00:30:42.166
You burrow through the
placenta, grab the foot,

00:30:42.166 --> 00:30:45.299
and slowly bring the
breech into the opening,

00:30:45.300 --> 00:30:50.333
just the same as you do
when delivering from below.

00:30:50.333 --> 00:30:54.066
If, after the
placenta is delivered

00:30:54.066 --> 00:30:58.999
the bed of the placenta bleeds,
you simply sew it up like this.

00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:02.366
You see it is very easy
to stop the bleeding.

00:31:02.366 --> 00:31:14.066
You lip over the bed of the placenta with number 0 catgut.

00:31:14.066 --> 00:31:17.899
Regarding infected
cases, we have not

00:31:17.900 --> 00:31:20.866
broadened the indication
for laparotrachelotomy

00:31:20.866 --> 00:31:24.599
to cover the frankly
infected case.

00:31:24.600 --> 00:31:28.433
But we have risked it,
even when the bag of waters

00:31:28.433 --> 00:31:30.833
has been ruptured a long time,

00:31:30.833 --> 00:31:33.999
when several vaginal examinations have been made,

00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:37.300
when labor has been prolonged, and when forceps

00:31:37.300 --> 00:31:43.033
has been attempted, providing there was a reasonable amount of cleanliness.

00:31:43.033 --> 00:31:48.566
The Porro operation is still the best for the frankly infected patients.

00:31:48.566 --> 00:31:52.266
But, although it is sad to have to say it,

00:31:52.266 --> 00:31:58.132
craniotomy may still be considered in rare instances.

00:31:58.133 --> 00:32:00.166
Local anesthesia.

00:32:00.166 --> 00:32:03.566
Local anesthesia has
helped materially

00:32:03.566 --> 00:32:06.732
to reduce our
maternal mortality.

00:32:06.733 --> 00:32:10.333
It is better than
spinal in every way.

00:32:10.333 --> 00:32:13.566
And even the neurologists
are telling us

00:32:13.566 --> 00:32:17.366
of late diseases resulting
from this invasion

00:32:17.366 --> 00:32:19.599
of the spinal canal.

00:32:19.600 --> 00:32:25.100
Laparotrachelotomy is
the ideal cesarean.

00:32:25.100 --> 00:32:29.566
And experience the world over has justified

00:32:29.566 --> 00:32:32.166
all the claims we have made for it.

00:32:32.166 --> 00:32:34.966
You remember I told
you that it would

00:32:34.966 --> 00:32:37.199
cut your mortality in half?

00:32:37.200 --> 00:32:44.133
Well, look at this chart.

00:32:44.133 --> 00:32:49.999
City of Chicago,
1934, 490 classics.

00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:53.300
Deaths, five and a half percent.

00:32:53.300 --> 00:32:59.333
Laparotrachelotomies, 541, two percent.

00:32:59.333 --> 00:33:04.099
Germany, classics 438.

00:33:04.100 --> 00:33:07.166
Deaths, six and four-tenths percent.

00:33:07.166 --> 00:33:10.966
Laparotrachelotomies, 3,554.

00:33:10.966 --> 00:33:14.032
Deaths, three and seven-tenths percent.

00:33:14.033 --> 00:33:18.799
Chicago Lying-In
Hospital, 1914 to 1936.

00:33:18.800 --> 00:33:21.733
Out of 60,000 deliveries--

00:33:21.733 --> 00:33:28.599
60,000 deliveries--classics 168, deaths six percent.

00:33:28.600 --> 00:33:35.000
Laparotrachelotomies, eighteen hundred and eleven...one-thousand eight hundred eleven.

00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:38.600
Deaths, 18 from all causes.

00:33:38.600 --> 00:33:47.133
Tuberculosis, eclampsia, heart disease, et cetera, one percent.

00:33:47.133 --> 00:33:54.866
Now ladies and
gentlemen, a final word.

00:33:54.866 --> 00:33:58.332
I believe in view of all these facts,

00:33:58.333 --> 00:34:02.399
that I may in all fairness
ask you this question.

00:34:02.400 --> 00:34:06.500
Does a man, in performing the old classic cesarean section,

00:34:06.500 --> 00:34:11.200
when the low cervical operation could be done,

00:34:11.200 --> 00:34:14.500
does he give his
patient all the benefits

00:34:14.500 --> 00:34:21.833
of modern obstetric art?

00:34:21.833 --> 00:34:35.833
[Music]

